# Cloudflare Tunnel Integration Plan

Expose CasaOS and the Flask app to the internet using a Cloudflare Tunnel and a custom domain.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> You will need to perform the following manual steps:
> 1. Run `cloudflared tunnel login` in your terminal and follow the link to authorize your domain.
> 2. Once authorized, I will need the **Domain Name** you want to use.
> 3. I will also need to know if you want to use subdomains (e.g., `casa.domain.com` and `api.domain.com`) or paths.

## Proposed Changes

### [NEW] Cloudflare Configuration

I will create a configuration file for `cloudflared` to route traffic.

#### [NEW] `cloudflared-config.yml` (file:///c:/projects/github/casaos-home-server/cloudflared-config.yml)
This file will define the tunnel behavior and service routing.

```yaml
tunnel: <tunnel-id>
credentials-file: /home/<user>/.cloudflared/<tunnel-id>.json

ingress:
  - hostname: <domain>
    service: http://localhost:80
  - hostname: api.<domain>
    service: http://localhost:5000
  - service: http_status:404
```

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
1. Run `cloudflared tunnel info` to check tunnel connectivity.
2. Run `cloudflared tunnel ingress validate` to verify the configuration file.

### Manual Verification
1. Access `https://<domain>` in a browser to see the CasaOS dashboard.
2. Access `https://api.<domain>` to see the Flask app's "Merhaba CasaOS!" message.
